# Django Router

Canon: `AGENTS.md`, then `documents/ai/manuals/django.md`.

Use when editing `django_apps/**`, `config/**`, or `manage.py`.

Rules:

- Keep views thin; put business logic in services/model methods.
- Prefer CBV unless FBV is clearly simpler.
- Use ORM; avoid raw SQL unless justified.
- Preserve signatures unless user asks.
- Use `select_related` / `prefetch_related` for N+1 risk.
- Do not add raw JSON/blob domain storage without current approval and tests.
- Contract changes need plan, acceptance, and tests.
- Templates display data; no business policy in templates.

Verify focused app tests plus lint/type gates from `AGENTS.md`.

References: `documents/ai/manuals/django.md`, `documents/ai/manuals/database.md`.
